  ('CS 101', 'Introduction to Computer Science', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Philosophy', '200 Level', 'first', 2, 'Concepts of hardware and software; basic subsystems of a digital computer; characteristics of a digital computer; devices/media; types/classes of computer emphasising the PC; history of computers and their generations. Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program. Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming. Booting and shutdown; types of operating system; user interface; managing information, computer malware (virus, etc); computer network; internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc. Office applications; use of a statistical package and a database management system.', '["Concepts of hardware and software","basic subsystems of a digital computer","characteristics of a digital computer","devices/media","types/classes of computer emphasising the PC","history of computers and their generations","Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program","Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming","Booting and shutdown","types of operating system","user interface","managing information, computer malware (virus, etc)","computer network","internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc","Office applications","use of a statistical package and a database management system"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Computer Science course outline'),
